+    protection:
+      ref: F1
+      kind: polyfuse
+-     what: "Bourns MF-MSMF200, 2.0 A hold, 3.5 A trip, 1812"
+-     rating_a: 2.0
++     what: "Bourns MF-MSMF110, 1.1 A hold, 2.2 A trip, 1812 (MF-MSMF110-2, JLCPCB C89647)"
++     rating_a: 1.1
+      interrupting_a: null
+      i2t_a2s: null
+-     basis: "v2/vendor/power/bourns-mf-msmf-pptc.pdf: the plain MF-MSMF200 is not in the table, whose rows are /8X, /12X and /16X, all of them 2.00 A hold, 3.50 A trip and 100 A maximum fault, differing only in maximum voltage, the lowest of which (8 V) clears this 5 V rail. A PPTC LIMITS rather than interrupts, so it declares no breaking capacity"
++     basis: "v2/vendor/power/bourns-mf-msmf-pptc.pdf: the plain MF-MSMF110 is not a row of the table, whose MF-MSMF110 rows are /8X, /16X, /16, /24X and /33X, every one 1.10 A hold and 2.20 A trip, differing in maximum voltage (8 to 33 V, the lowest of which clears this 5 V rail), maximum fault current (100 A for /8X, /16X and /16, 20 A for /24X and /33X) and R1max (0.18 to 0.21 Ohm); '-2 = Tape and Reel' (How to Order). Thermal Derating Table: 0.85 A at 50 C, 0.77 A at 60 C and 0.71 A at 70 C (/8X, /16X), so board C's 0.6 A continuous holds inside the sealed case and its 1.0 A must stay a peak. A PPTC LIMITS rather than interrupts, so it declares no breaking capacity"
+    protects: null
+-   note: "the panel's 5 V, and the stage where the fuse is chosen for the lead rather than for the track: 2.0 A of hold against 1.23 A of copper at 10 K"
++   note: "the panel's 5 V. Since MESHSAT-1357 round 8 (board B author, 26 September 2026) the fuse is chosen for the track: 1.1 A of hold against 1.23 A of copper at 10 K, where the MF-MSMF200 held 2.0 A (PWR-003's finding of 17 September, closed on the part; the 0.8 mm PANEL class of gen_pcb_b3.py stays for the next cut)"
+ 
+  - id: B_HDMI_5V
+    fed_by: BOARD_A_CONVERTERS
+@@ -302,12 +302,6 @@ stages:
+ 
+ # THE FAILURES THIS CHAIN CARRIES, each with its sentence. A gate that fails is doing its job; a failure nobody
+ # has written down is a different thing, so the suite accepts exactly the ones named here and refuses a new one.
+-known_findings:
+-  - stage: B_PANEL_5V
+-    why: "board B's panel 5 V carries a 2.0 A hold, 3.5 A trip polyfuse on a 0.4 mm PWR-class track that
+-      IPC-2221 rates at 1.23 A at 10 K and 1.67 at 20 K, feeding a 0.6 A rail with a 1.0 A peak: the copper is
+-      the weaker element and a fault at the panel end would run at the fuse's trip current through it. Found on
+-      17 September 2026, while board B was mid-route on B21, so the copper cannot change in this phase. The two
+-      answers are a wider conductor (0.8 mm is 2.03 A at 10 K, which clears the hold) or a smaller part
+-      (MF-MSMF110 holds 1.1 A and trips at 2.2, which clears the track and leaves ten percent over board C's
+-      declared 1.0 A peak), and B22 is where either lands. Nothing here is waived: PWR-003 fails on board B."
++# MESHSAT-1357 round 8 (26 September 2026): B_PANEL_5V, the one finding this list carried since 17 September, is closed on
++# the part (F1 is an MF-MSMF110, 1.1 A hold, under the 1.23 A track); the list is empty until the gate finds another.
++known_findings: []
+diff --git a/v2/ecad/tools/tests/test_energy_chain.py b/v2/ecad/tools/tests/test_energy_chain.py
+index 3546b842..baf4367f 100644
+--- a/v2/ecad/tools/tests/test_energy_chain.py
++++ b/v2/ecad/tools/tests/test_energy_chain.py
+@@ -322,14 +322,20 @@ def t_a_branch_declares_what_feeds_it_rather_than_being_known_by_name():
+ 
+ def t_the_panel_branch_is_the_finding_it_should_be():
+     """The reading this stage was added for, kept as a rule so a later change cannot make it quietly disappear:
+-    board B's panel 5 V carries a 2.0 A hold polyfuse on a 0.4 mm class track, and IPC-2221 gives that track
++    board B's panel 5 V carried a 2.0 A hold polyfuse on a 0.4 mm class track, and IPC-2221 gives that track
+     1.23 A at 10 K. Either the copper widens or the part changes; what may not happen is the pair going
+-    unremarked."""
+-    import yaml
++    unremarked. MESHSAT-1357 round 8 (26 September 2026): THE PART CHANGED. F1 is a Bourns MF-MSMF110 (1.1 A
++    hold) in board B's generator and in this chain, so the stage now sits under its copper; the rule keeps the
++    two in step, so a return to a larger part, or a chain line that no longer names the part the board carries,
++    fails here."""
++    import yaml, re
+     chain = yaml.safe_load(open(os.path.join(TOOLS, "pcb_energy_chain.yaml"), encoding="utf-8"))
+     st = [s for s in chain["stages"] if s["id"] == "B_PANEL_5V"]
+     assert st, "board B's panel branch is not in the chain at all"
+     s = st[0]
+-    assert float(s["protection"]["rating_a"]) > float(s["conductor"]["rating_a"]), \
+-        "the stage no longer carries the finding: check whether the copper was widened or the part changed, " \
+-        "and say which in the note here"
++    assert float(s["protection"]["rating_a"]) < float(s["conductor"]["rating_a"]), \
++        "the panel fuse is above its track again: the copper or the part changed; say which in the note here"
++    assert "MF-MSMF110" in s["protection"]["what"], s["protection"]["what"]
++    gen = open(os.path.join(TOOLS, "gen_sch_b.py"), encoding="utf-8").read()
++    f1 = re.search(r'part\("F1", "Device", "Polyfuse", "([^"]+)"', gen)
++    assert f1 and "MF-MSMF110" in f1.group(1), "board B's F1 no longer names the part the chain declares: %r" % (f1 and f1.group(1))
